       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is twice the usual maximum dose of 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood pressure benefit.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, a typical starting dose. You could titrate up to 10 mg after 1\u20132 weeks.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written.** If you really intend this dose, for example as a specialist-directed plan, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it exceeds the usual maximum.\n\nIf blood pressure is still uncontrolled at 10 mg, adding a second agent such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide diuretic is usually preferred over going higher on amlodipine."
      }
     ],
